job_description:
⚪ Job Description
At Octopus Energy Trading, we’re on a mission to reshape the future of energy. As part of Octopus Energy Group, we’re creating an innovative approach to trading that will accelerate the transition to a Net Zero world. With the growth of renewables and a push toward decarbonising heating and transport, greater flexibility in the grid is essential. We are building cutting-edge technology to optimise everything from domestic EV charging to grid-scale batteries, to meet the global demand for energy flexibility. We’re looking for passionate and unconventional thinkers to join us on this journey, bringing a diversity of experience and ideas to shape a more efficient, flexible, and sustainable energy system. With an increase in variable and distributed supply, using data for trading and forecasting has never been more important. Octopus has always had a tech-first approach, and our trading and analytics tools are all built in-house. We are looking for a data scientist who’s comfortable building data pipelines bringing together internal and external data to create market leading insights using both classical and ML techniques. This will include looking at demand, renewables and transmission system fundamentals forecasts focussed to begin with on the GB intraday power market.
🟡 What You'll Do...
Exploring the types of data needed to effectively trade the GB intraday power market
Building, improving and maintaining models to forecast electricity demand and renewable generation, primarily in GB but developing into all of Western Europe;
Finding high quality, novel data sources to base our forecasts off of;
Development on forecasting framework and tools;
Maintaining and automating forecasting processes, whilst building in checks and alerting;
Utilising these forecasting models to build or enhance our price forecasts
Collaborating with Trading, Renewables, Flexibility and other teams to utilise our combined knowledge and data.
🟢 What You'll Need...
Experience with Python is essential;
A good understanding of what forecasting techniques to use and the ability to build a simple baseline and quickly iterate;
Ability to communicate your approach, including its strengths and limitations;
Able to quickly understand commercial and industry concepts;
Team player excited at the idea of ownership across lots of different projects and tools;
Passion for driving towards Net Zero;
Experience with Machine Learning is essential;
Experience in the electricity industry in GB would be useful but not required.

# HVAC Service Engineer
* Location: Perth - Covering local council areas in accordance with our current contracts
* Contract: Full Time | Permanent
* Salary: Competitive
## Job description
## About JGM
Welcome to John G Mackintosh (JGM).
Founded in 1907 as a small family-run business, John G Mackintosh has grown steadily over the years, guided by values that remain central to our success today: Integrity, Diligence, Professionalism, and Collaboration. These principles define our culture and shape the way we work with colleagues, clients, and partners.
Our vision is to be Scotland’s preferred choice for building services solutions, and every member of the JGM team contributes to achieving that goal.
JGM delivers high-quality building services solutions across multiple sectors, supporting clients through safe, reliable, and high-performing engineering delivery.
We are proud to be an equal opportunities employer, committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination, where everyone is treated with respect and fairness.
JGM is committed to equality, diversity, and inclusion and welcomes applications from all suitably qualified candidates.
## Role Overview
We are seeking an experienced and motivated HVAC Service Engineer to join our growing Building Services team. The successful candidate will be responsible for the servicing, maintenance, fault diagnosis and repair of a wide range of commercial heating, ventilation and air conditioning systems across our client portfolio.
This is an excellent opportunity for an engineer who takes pride in delivering high-quality workmanship and exceptional customer service while developing their career within a progressive and supportive organisation.
## Health, Safety & Environment
Safety is a core value at JGM and must always be a primary consideration in all work activities.
All employees have a responsibility to under the Health & Safety at Work Act 1974 to:
* Take reasonable care of themselves and others who may be affected by their actions or omissions;
* Ensure the health, safety, and welfare of colleagues and visitors;
* Protect, as far as reasonably practicable, others from risks arising from work activities.
All duties must be carried out in accordance with company Health, Safety, and Environmental policies and procedures.
## Key Responsibilities
* Carry out planned preventative maintenance (PPM) on HVAC systems in accordance with maintenance schedules;
* Diagnose faults and undertake reactive repairs on HVAC and associated mechanical building services equipment;
* Service and maintain air conditioning systems including split, multi-split, VRV/VRF and heat pump systems;
* Inspect, maintain and repair ventilation systems, air handling units, extract systems and associated plant;
* Complete service reports, certification and documentation accurately using digital reporting systems;
* Ensure all works are completed safely and in compliance with current legislation, industry standards and company procedures;
* Liaise professionally with clients, providing technical advice where appropriate;
* Participate in the on-call rota as required.
## Skills & Competencies
### Essential
* Proven experience servicing and maintaining commercial HVAC systems;
* F-Gas Category 1 Certification. (In house training will be provided);
* NVQ Level 2/3, City & Guilds or equivalent qualification in HVAC or Mechanical Engineering;
* Strong fault-finding and diagnostic skills;
* Good understanding of health and safety legislation and safe systems of work;
* Full UK Driving Licence;
* Excellent communication and customer service skills;
* Ability to work independently and as part of a team.
### Desirable
* Experience working within commercial buildings across sectors such as healthcare, education, retail and industrial;
* IPAF and PASMA certifications;
* Knowledge of BMS controls and HVAC control systems;
* Experience using digital job management systems.
## What We Offer
* Company van and fuel card;
* Company pension scheme;
* Company mobile phone and tablet;
* Ongoing technical and manufacturer training;
* Career progression opportunities;
* A supportive and collaborative working environment.
## Application Process
To apply, please submit your CV together with a short covering letter outlining your relevant experience and qualifications.
Applications should be sent to: careers@jgm.co.uk
If you would like to discuss the role before applying, please contact **James Hendry**on **07771 626 924.**
## Closing Date
### **14th August 2026**
Early applications are encouraged, as we reserve the right to close the vacancy once a suitable candidate has been appointed.

# Legal Counsel, Banking - Vice President
Apply now »
**Date:** 24 Jul 2026
**Location:**
London (Lon), GB
**Company:** Mizuho
**Profile Summary**
This is a wide-ranging role for a commercially minded banking lawyer, with responsibility for providing legal advice under English law for the Japanese corporate client business of Mizuho Bank Ltd., London Branch, Mizuho International plc and Mizuho Bank Europe N.V. (“MBE”) and their respective branches and subsidiaries within the EMEA region;
**Duties and Responsibilities**
* The role includes providing legal support on bilateral and syndicated loans, guarantees and a wide range of corporate and transaction banking products offered to Japanese corporates (including not just LMA based lending i.e. more complex bespoke loan products e.g. loans with structured interest rates), while working closely with front office, credit, risk and operations teams;
* Provide legal support to Loan Capital Markets (Distribution) desk for credit risk insurance business;
* Back-up support / coverage for Trade Finance matters of the Japanese client business including facilities under which different instruments can be issued e.g. guarantees, letters of credit or bonds etc; deposits, account documentation, cash management;
* Provide legal support to front office and MBE middle office for an intra-group capital risk transfer scheme for loans from time to time; and
* Advise and assist Head Office in Tokyo and other Mizuho group entities on general English law matters from time to time;
and:
* Ensure any external counsel required to support on any transactions are appropriately instructed and supervised;
* Ensure appropriate records are maintained for the Legal Department, including the data bases, directories and documentation management necessary to record transactions / matters worked on; and
* Support their manager to ensure know-how, policies, procedures and playbooks are maintained and reviewed at least annually and in response to any material developments.
**Qualifications, Skills, and Experience**
* Qualified solicitor of at least 3-4 years’ PQE, with experience gained through an international bank, a law firm with a banking practice or a combination of the two;
* Strong technical expertise in corporate banking law and regulation, including strong understanding of LMA and other relevant documentation frameworks;
* Strong client service orientation;
* Great organisational and time management skills;
* Excellent communication, negotiation and stakeholder management skills;
* Demonstrable ability to innovate, support change and problem solve;
* Demonstrable commercial judgment, balancing commercial objectives and legal risk;
* Ability to work independently, while recognising where escalation is appropriate;
* Knowledge of banking and financial services is an advantage;
* High attention to detail;
* Cultural awareness and ability to work effectively with colleagues across different jurisdictions; and
* Collaborative nature to contribute to a successful team and departmental performance, fostering the spirit of teamwork and cohesiveness.
**What Mizuho can offer you**
Here at Mizuho, there are fantastic progression opportunities and clear paths to promotion. We will give you ample opportunity to affect change and to help grow our business.
In addition to the great opportunity outlined above we are also currently able to offer:
* Competitive starting salary, plus discretionary bonus
* Non-contributory pension
* 27 days’ annual leave
* Core working hours\*
* Hybrid working - office and home based\*
* Virtual GP
* Wellbeing benefits, including Mental Health Allies and First Aiders
\**For applicable roles only*
**At Mizuho, we embrace flexible ways of working when the role permits. We offer different working arrangements like part-time, job-sharing and hybrid (office and home) working. Our purpose-led culture and global infrastructure help us connect, collaborate, and work together in agile ways to meet all our business needs.**
**At Mizuho we are committed to supporting equality, diversity and equality, and seek to create a workplace that is fully inclusive. We welcome applications from all sections of the community that we operate in and from all ethnic backgrounds, sexual orientation, beliefs, gender identities and disabilities.**
**If you require more information about our equal opportunities policy or wish to discuss any accessibility requirements or reasonable adjustments please contact the recruitment team – recruitment@mizuhoemea.com and we will be happy to help.**

# Legal Counsel, Derivatives - Vice President
Apply now »
**Date:** 29 Jul 2026
**Location:**
London (Lon), GB
**Company:** Mizuho
**Profile Summary**
We are seeking a commercially minded and technically strong lawyer to join our Derivatives and Structured Finance Legal team as a Vice President. The successful candidate will provide legal support to Mizuho’s derivatives business across EMEA, advising on a broad range of OTC derivatives transactions, particularly finance linked derivatives transactions, and related regulatory matters.
The role will focus principally on negotiating and advising on ISDA documentation and supporting Mizuho EMEA’s business promotion, trading and treasury businesses, particularly the Derivatives Risk Solutions EMEA group. Experience of securities financing transactions, including repurchase transactions and securities lending under the GMRA and GMSLA, would be advantageous.
This is a business facing role requiring sound legal judgment, strong drafting and negotiation skills and the ability to manage multiple stakeholders in an investment banking environment.
**Duties and Responsibilities**
Provide legal support to Mizuho Bank Ltd., London Branch, Mizuho International plc and Mizuho Bank Europe N.V. and their respective branches and subsidiaries within the EMEA region as follows:
* Negotiate, draft, structure and advise on a wide range of derivatives documentation used by the, including:
+ ISDA Master Agreements (1992 and 2002);
+ Credit Support Annexes (English, New York and other forms);
+ IM documentation and collateral arrangements;
+ ISDA Resolution Stay Protocols and related adherence documentation;
+ Cleared derivatives documentation, including client clearing agreements;
+ FBF and DRV, with support from French and German counsel, respectively; and
+ Certain structured rate lending agreements.
* Advise front office, sales and trading, operations, credit risk, collateral management and other support functions on legal issues arising from derivatives trading.
* Provide legal advice on new products, transaction structures and strategic initiatives.
* Monitor for and support implementation of legal and regulatory change affecting derivatives markets, including new ISDA definitions, EMIR, UK EMIR, Dodd-Frank, MiFID II, SFTR, CDSR and other applicable regulations;
* Advise on close-out, default, netting and collateral enforcement issues;
* Work closely with credit, risk and compliance teams on legal risk management;
* Contribute to internal legal policies, template documentation and legal training;
* Support legal projects, regulatory remediation exercises and documentation repapering exercises;
* (Desirable but not essential) Provide legal support in relation to GMRA, GMSLA, margin lending and other collateral arrangements;
and:
* Ensure any external counsel required to support on any transactions are appropriately instructed and supervised;
* Ensure appropriate records are maintained for Legal Services, including the data bases, directories and documentation management necessary to record transactions / matters worked on; and
* Support their manager to ensure know-how, policies, procedures and playbooks are maintained and reviewed at least annually and in response to any material developments.
**Qualifications, Skills, and Experience**
* Qualified solicitor of at least 4-8 years’ PQE, with experience gained through an international bank, a law firm with a derivatives or structured finance practice or a combination of the two;
* Strong technical expertise in derivatives law and regulation, including strong understanding of ISDA documentation for corporate clients and counterparties;
* Technical expertise with GMRA and / or GMSLA master agreements is an advantage;
* Strong client service orientation;
* Great organisational and time management skills, with ability to manage competing priorities and deadlines;
* Excellent communication, negotiation and stakeholder management skills;
* Demonstrable ability to innovate, support change and problem solve;
* Demonstrable commercial judgment, balancing commercial objectives and legal risk;
* Ability to work independently, while recognising where escalation is appropriate;
* Knowledge of financial services and structured finance is an advantage;
* High attention to detail;
* Cultural awareness and ability to work effectively with colleagues across different jurisdictions; and
* Collaborative nature to contribute to a successful team and departmental performance, fostering the spirit of teamwork and cohesiveness.
**What Mizuho can offer you**
Here at Mizuho, there are fantastic progression opportunities and clear paths to promotion. We will give you ample opportunity to affect change and to help grow our business.
In addition to the great opportunity outlined above we are also currently able to offer:
* Competitive starting salary, plus discretionary bonus
* Non-contributory pension
* 27 days’ annual leave
* Core working hours\*
* Hybrid working - office and home based\*
* Virtual GP
* Wellbeing benefits, including Mental Health Allies and First Aiders
\**For applicable roles only*
**At Mizuho, we embrace flexible ways of working when the role permits. We offer different working arrangements like part-time, job-sharing and hybrid (office and home) working. Our purpose-led culture and global infrastructure help us connect, collaborate, and work together in agile ways to meet all our business needs.**
**At Mizuho we are committed to supporting equality, diversity and equality, and seek to create a workplace that is fully inclusive. We welcome applications from all sections of the community that we operate in and from all ethnic backgrounds, sexual orientation, beliefs, gender identities and disabilities.**
**If you require more information about our equal opportunities policy or wish to discuss any accessibility requirements or reasonable adjustments please contact the recruitment team – recruitment@mizuhoemea.com and we will be happy to help.**
